      "standardized_narrative": "At 1 January 2019 the Syndicate's gross claims outstanding (claims reserves) stood at GBP 830.4m. The report does not disclose a single aggregate GROSS prioryear development number; the 2017 Year of Account was reinsured to close into 2018 (RITC premium GBP 219.3m) and closed at the end of 2019 with a loss (2.71% of capacity), which distorts development comparators. The Syndicate highlights material gross exposures to a number of catastrophe events (e.g. Typhoon Hagibis and Faxai in 2019 and Hurricane Michael, Typhoon Jebi, the Camp and Woolsey wildfires and the Lurssen shipyard loss in 2018) with mixed movements by line - some lines (notably Third party liability and parts of casualty/A&H) strengthened, while Property and Marine showed releases in the year-end gross outstanding balances overall.",
